mas"},"3961":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones-6","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones","content":"Steam añade una ruta de transporte y servicios de plataforma, pero no resuelve automáticamente los problemas de networking del juego."},"3962":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones-7","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones#steam-no-sustituye-un-servidor-autoritativo","content":"Puedes transportar una sesión P2P y mantener un jugador como autoridad de gameplay. La arquitectura del juego es independiente del medio de transporte."},"3963":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones-8","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones#steam-no-sustituye-un-lobby-eco","content":"Rich Presence puede facilitar descubrimiento y unión, pero el estado del lobby debe seguir viviendo en Eco si contiene reglas de partida."},"3964":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones-9","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones#steam-no-sustituye-autenticación-de-gameplay","content":"El Steam ID identifica al usuario de la plataforma. El servidor debe decidir qué puede hacer ese usuario dentro de la partida."},"3965":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones-10","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones#steam-no-sustituye-persistencia","content":"Guardar una partida sigue siendo responsabilidad del juego y de sus mecanismos de persistencia."},"3966":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones-11","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones#plataformas","content":"La integración está condicionada por compilación y no debe asumirse disponible en plataformas donde el bloque Steam no se compile. fileciteturn190file0"},"3967":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones-12","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/limitaciones#plataformas","content":"Diseña una abstracción de identidad/transporte para que el gameplay no dependa directamente de Steam. Steam debe ser una implementación de plataforma, no la arquitectura completa de red."},"3968":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas","type":"page","content":"Lobby y partidas","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Red","Red","Contenido","Steam"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas"},"3969":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas-0","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas","content":"Diseñar el flujo de lobby sin mezclar Steam con el estado de gameplay de Eco."},"3970":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas-1","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas#separación-recomendada","content":"Separación recomendada"},"3971":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas-2","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas#flujo-cooperativo","content":"Flujo cooperativo"},"3972":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas-3","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas#por-qué-no-usar-steam-como-autoridad","content":"Por qué no usar Steam como autoridad"},"3973":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas-4","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas#hasta-cuatro-jugadores","content":"Hasta cuatro jugadores"},"3974":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas-5","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas","content":"Steam puede facilitar descubrimiento y unión, pero el lobby de gameplay debe seguir teniendo un estado propio."},"3975":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas-6","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas#por-qué-no-usar-steam-como-autoridad","content":"Steam conoce la identidad y el transporte, pero no conoce las reglas de tu partida. Eco debe decidir si un jugador puede entrar, qué canal recibe y qué objetos se crean."},"3976":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas-7","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/lobby-y-partidas#hasta-cuatro-jugadores","content":"Para un juego cooperativo de cuatro jugadores, el límite de Steam y el límite de gameplay deben considerarse por separado. El servidor debe rechazar jugadores adicionales aunque el transporte permita técnicamente una conexión."},"3977":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo","type":"page","content":"Protocolo","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Red","Red","Contenido","Steam"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo"},"3978":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo-0","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo","content":"Qué parte del protocolo pertenece a Eco y qué parte a Steam."},"3979":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo-1","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo#ventaja","content":"Ventaja"},"3980":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo-2","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo#limitación-conceptual","content":"Limitación conceptual"},"3981":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo-3","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo","content":"La integración Steam no reemplaza el protocolo de Eco. Implementa un transporte que satisface `IConnection`."},"3982":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo-4","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo","content":"La clase `P2PConnection` recibe un `Buffer`, extrae paquetes completos y los envía al Steam ID remoto. Al desconectarse, genera el estado de desconexión que Eco puede procesar. fileciteturn190file0"},"3983":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo-5","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo#ventaja","content":"El código de gameplay no necesita conocer si un paquete viaja por TCP, UDP o Steam P2P. La capa de transporte mantiene esa decisión aislada."},"3984":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo-6","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo#limitación-conceptual","content":"Cambiar el transporte no elimina los problemas de diseño del protocolo. Tamaño de paquetes, frecuencia, serialización, ownership, destinatarios y autoridad siguen siendo responsabilidad de la arquitectura Eco."},"3985":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo-7","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/protocolo#limitación-conceptual","content":"Steam proporciona el camino. Eco define qué se transmite y el juego define qué significa."},"3986":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/rich-presence","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/rich-presence","type":"page","content":"Rich Presence","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Red","Red","Contenido","Steam"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/rich-presence"},"3987":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/rich-presence-0","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/rich-presence","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/steam/rich-presence","content":"Utilizar la presencia de Steam para anunciar el estado de conexión."},"3988":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/rich-presence-1","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/steam/rich-presence","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/st